NAME
     df - how much of each file system is used

SYNOPSIS
     df [-h] [-i] [PATH...]

DESCRIPTION
     df prints one line per mounted file system: what it is, how big it
     is, how much is used and free, and where it is mounted. With a PATH
     it prints the one that PATH is on.

OPTIONS
     -h   kilobytes and megabytes rather than blocks
     -i   inodes rather than blocks

SEE ALSO
     du(1), mount(1), stat(1)
